                <pb facs="0843" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg755"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports the decision of the prize court confiscating all the cargo
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">Arabia</hi> consigned to Japan and the release of
                    the vessel and the balance of the cargo, and that the attention of the minister
                    for foreign affairs has been called to the discrepancy in the decision
                    confiscating the cargo while not mentioning it as contraband.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
